From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 15:17:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] inetcomm: Register the MIME classes Windows registers for
 what it implements.

Saving a single file web page (MHT), Word first looks for
CLSID_IMimePropertySchema in the registry, and without it tells the
user to install Outlook Express or Windows Mail, in a message box that
DisplayAlerts does not hold back: the save never happened, and an
automated one waited for ever.  With the class there Word writes the
MIME document itself.

Windows registers 31 classes for inetcomm.dll.  Of those Wine
implements CLSID_IMimePropertySchema (the object MimeOleGetPropertySchema
gives), CLSID_IMimeInternational, CLSID_IMimePropertySet (the body
object) and CLSID_IMimeMessageTree (the message object) without
registering them or having a factory for them; now it does.  The
international object the class makes is one of its own, as in Windows,
not the one MimeOleGetInternat gives.  The test passes on Windows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit d9f12b31109f7463cdb386c88abc2f1fa3264888)

